# Non-secret defaults, shared by every deployment. THIS FILE IS COMMITTED.
#
# The split: anything safe to read in a public repository lives here, anything that
# would burn if it leaked lives in .env.local, which is not committed and which
# .env.example is the template for. Nothing in this file is a credential.
#
# Next looks a variable up in process.env, then .env.local, then .env, and stops at the
# first hit. So a value here is a DEFAULT: the host overrides it by setting a real
# environment variable, and you override it locally in .env.local, without either of
# them editing this file.

# Which deployment this is: LOCAL, STAGING or PRODUCTION.
# Read once in src/server/serverConfig.ts, which falls back to LOCAL for anything unset
# or unrecognised — including a lowercase "production", since the check is membership
# of the Env enum rather than a cast.
#
# LOCAL is the right default for a clone, and it is the wrong value in production:
# `secure` on the visitor cookie is set from `serverConfig.env !== Env.Local`, so a
# production host that never sets ENV hands out its visitor cookie without the Secure
# flag. Set ENV=PRODUCTION on the host, where it belongs, not here.
ENV=LOCAL

# The public playlist /lab/suggest reads and writes to.
#
# OPTIONAL, and not a secret: it is in the address bar of a public page. It defaults to
# SUGGEST_PLAYLIST_ID in src/constants/suggest.ts, so a clone renders the real playlist
# with nothing set. Point a deployment somewhere else by setting it on that host, which
# is how you keep staging's test adds off the playlist jaako actually listens to.
#
# `pnpm playlist:id <url>` turns a Spotify share link into the value that goes here.
# SPOTIFY_PLAYLIST_ID=
